What is a [Java code] solution for validating whether a given string is a palindrome or not? 
Please provide a code snippet using Java that checks whether a given string is a palindrome or not. A palindrome is a word, phrase, number, or other sequence of characters that reads the same forward and backward. To check for a palindrome, you can use the following code:
```java
public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
    int i = 0, j = str.length() - 1;
    while (i < j) {
        if (str.charAt(i) != str.charAt(j)) {
            return false;
        }
        i++;
        j--;
    }
    return true;
}
```
This code will return `true` if the input string is a palindrome and `false` otherwise.

